  "description": "The application is for one tree which is a sycamore. It is the only tree in the garden at 37A (Basement) Edbrooke Road and is located in the south east corner of the garden immediately next to the boundary wall with Edbrooke Road Gardens. The tree was last cut back in 2014 and has clearly grown a great deal in the period since. It now covers an unreasonably large area of the garden.\r\rThe application is to crown reduce (by approx 2m) and lift (to min 2.5m above ground) to the previous, most recent reduction points, retaining shortened furnishing growth and at least 50% of fine branch structure to maintain crown continuity.",
